{"title":"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Use_Answer_Choices_to_our_advantage)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Use Answer Choices to our advantage)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Fractions)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Fractions)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_ANALYSIS!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE ANALYSIS!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Bella begins to walk from her house toward her friend Ella's house. At the same time, Ella begins to ride her bicycle toward Bella's house. They each maintain a constant speed, and Ella rides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times as fast as Bella walks. The distance between their houses is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d3b5ec02214174f7f77be34664e65a90496eb15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10,560$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> feet, and Bella covers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e01d39c002ec80f99eed43b6da372e77b856ce5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\tfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"18\" height=\"21\" /> feet with each step. How many steps will Bella take by the time she meets Ella?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/8/068122af11acb54b2dcf5af10505fdca9ddb8906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }704\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }845\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }1056\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }1760\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }3520$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"470\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Solution 1 (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Every 10 feet Bella goes, Ella goes 50 feet, which means a total of 60 feet. They need to travel that 60 feet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bd82fe8adf4cefa5fc23c8f463b18b009c43233.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10560\\div60=176$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" /> times to travel the entire 2 miles. Since Bella goes 10 feet 176 times, this means that she travels a total of 1760 feet. And since she walks 2.5 feet each step, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084003a88534a99b40fb71d87c8366d46d17e16e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1760\\div2.5=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }704}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"182\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Use_Answer_Choices_to_our_advantage.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Use_Answer_Choices_to_our_advantage)\">Solution 2 (Use Answer Choices to our advantage)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Use Answer Choices to our advantage)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that Bella goes 2.5 feet per step and since Ella rides 5 times faster than Bella she must go 12.5 feet on her bike for every step of Bella's. For Bella and Ella to meet, the total distance they cover together must be 10,560 feet, so each step of Bella's closes 2.5 + 12.5 = 15 feet of the gap between them. \n</p><p>Now we can test the answer choices. If Bella takes 704 steps, together they cover 704 * 15 = 10,560 feet, which is exactly the distance between the houses. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/157f2eb285169343b776513fb6d252e23ddb0fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }704}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"74\" height=\"28\" />.\n～minor edited\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Fractions.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Fractions)\">Solution 3 (Fractions)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Fractions)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can turn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e01d39c002ec80f99eed43b6da372e77b856ce5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\tfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"18\" height=\"21\" /> into an improper fraction. It will then become <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/d/3adf28c1ab96fc4eddaa890ec574e4cea2caea36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. Since Ella bikes 5 times faster, we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/5/81585cdf5f7bd47faaa0cd58d8788a50c517507e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot 5=\\frac{25}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />. Then we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d85d15696ae3984d4bcbc68e57ce86a3c44a999b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{25}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" /> to find the distance they walk and bike together for each step of Bella's: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68cae02fedbd39268572c8d44ec69d95e3e8dd1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30}{2} = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" />. This means that they travel 15 ft. of distance for each step that Bella takes. Divide 10,560 by 15 to find that Bella takes }704}$ steps.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_ANALYSIS.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_ANALYSIS!!!)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE ANALYSIS!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE ANALYSIS!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4xkFOM218Ro\">https://youtu.be/4xkFOM218Ro</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/TkZvMa30Juo?t=1123\">https://youtu.be/TkZvMa30Juo?t=1123</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ycZ381n_1bQ\">https://youtu.be/ycZ381n_1bQ</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UczCIsRzAeo\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UczCIsRzAeo</a>   ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8\" title=\"2018 AMC 8\">2018 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2018\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"